+## M5 - Unified dashboard and reproducibility (2026-11-18)
+
+- Single-page layout: Render M1 CNF satisfiability and the 0/1 linear bridge, M2
+  schedule comparison and weekly filters, M3 `{M, A, N, -}` DFA verification, and
+  M4 Direction B fairness/equilibrium plots on one page so active schedule changes
+  propagate immediately across all four modules without hidden state.
+- Clean-clone startup and solver bounds: Load `data/seed.txt`, the raw dataset,
+  `m2_ilp/schedule.csv`, and M3 DFA specs automatically on open; compute M4's
+  soft-threshold refinement in memory when `m4_dynamics/fatigue_aware_schedule.csv`
+  is absent without writing into M1–M4 directories. Restrict interactive CBC solves
+  to `toy` and `subset` slices under a bounded `time_limit`, while `full` mode
+  inspects precomputed or strictly validated uploaded schedules.
+- Slice calibration fallback: Pooled lag-one OLS in M4 requires at least two
+  weekly blocks; single-day `toy` or short custom slices fall back transparently
+  to `full_instance` baseline parameters `(a, b, r)` and report the calibration
+  source rather than fabricating physiological parameters.
+- Deterministic `m5` stage: `run_all.py --stage m5` calls `app.precompute.run_m5`
+  to cross-check M1–M4 invariants and emit a sorted, timestamp-free JSON summary
+  without mutating upstream artifacts or leaving untracked files in the checkout.
